Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: mt8901: add DSP duplex audio and SRAM ownership

Provide exclusive, aligned SRAM leases through the AFE owner on the
firmware-described SRAM layout. Each lease retains device, module and
runtime-PM references. Require retention votes for system sleep and
disable manual driver detachment. Published buffers remain retained
until reboot; whole-core quiesce and release are separate work.

Add opt-in DL0/DL1 playback and UL1 capture to the AFE/SoundWire route.
Copy playback commits and capture notifications through owned rings and
defer complete-period notifications to workqueue context. Synchronize
listeners and drain work before retiring borrowed ALSA pointers.
The duplex path is disabled by default and still needs complete hardware
streaming qualification.

---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/sound/mt8901-afe-sram.h
@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
+#ifndef MT8901_AFE_SRAM_H
+#define MT8901_AFE_SRAM_H
+
+#include <linux/compiler_types.h>
+#include <linux/types.h>
+
+struct device;
+struct snd_pcm_substream;
+struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer;
+
+struct mt8901_afe_sram_view {
+	void __iomem *area;
+	u64 cpu_address;
+	u64 afe_address;
+	u64 dsp_address;
+	size_t bytes;
+};
+
+struct mt8901_afe_sram_endpoint {
+	u32 abi_version;
+	struct mt8901_afe_sram_view memory;
+	u32 rate, channels, sample_bits, period_frames, periods;
+	u8 memif, irq;
+	bool published, irq_prepared;
+};
+
+/* Return a referenced, instantiated sound-card device for a real owned DL0/DL1
+ * playback or UL1 capture stream, or ERR_PTR(). No firmware or power operation. The caller
+ * serializes stream lifetime and must put_device() the returned reference.
+ */
+struct device *mt8901_afe_pcm_card_device(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream);
+
+/* Reserve and zero a multiple of 16 bytes from the AFE-owned SRAM pool.
+ * Holds a device, module and runtime-PM reference until an unpublished lease
+ * is released. Returns an exclusive handle or ERR_PTR(); sleeps.
+ */
+struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *mt8901_afe_sram_reserve(struct device *dev, size_t bytes);
+
+/* Reserve 1..4 KiB of IPC SRAM from a bound PCM lease's owner, in 1 KiB
+ * multiples. The caller serializes the peer's lifetime. The new lease has
+ * independent references and cannot bind a PCM substream. This call sleeps.
+ */
+struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *
+mt8901_afe_sram_reserve_ipc(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *peer, size_t bytes);
+
+/* Mark an IPC lease published before registering its address with firmware.
+ * Published IPC leases retain the same suspend/unload guards as PCM leases.
+ * They cannot be released until a verified DSP quiesce contract is added.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_publish_ipc(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer);
+
+/* Read the three address views for this allocation. The client selects the
+ * view required by its service protocol; these are not interchangeable DMA
+ * addresses. This copies metadata only and leaves the output unchanged on error.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_view(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer,
+			struct mt8901_afe_sram_view *view);
+
+/* Bind an unpublished lease during non-running PCM stream setup, after
+ * the AFE DAI's hw_params. Derives memif, IRQ and format from that substream;
+ * its complete ring must fit the reservation. A bound memif cannot start
+ * another substream until the lease is released. The caller serializes ALSA
+ * setup/teardown around this call. It does not program or start the memif.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_bind(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer,
+			 struct snd_pcm_substream *substream);
+
+/* Reattach a retired, published lease after acknowledged DSP HWFREE/CLOSE.
+ * The DSP owner alone may call this; it must serialize task and stream state.
+ * Allows DL0/DL1 playback rebinding or unchanged UL1 capture. Requires idle
+ * old/new IRQs and memifs, healthy owner state and a ring fitting the allocation.
+ * No memory or PM references are freed.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_rebind(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer,
+			   struct snd_pcm_substream *substream);
+
+/* Return a bound endpoint only while its original AFE substream still owns
+ * the memif and its format is unchanged. bytes must equal sizeof(*endpoint).
+ * The output is unchanged on error. This call sleeps.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_endpoint(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer,
+			    struct mt8901_afe_sram_endpoint *endpoint, size_t bytes);
+
+/* Program the published lease's memif address, checking each write.
+ * Requires non-running, unchanged ALSA setup, serialized by the caller.
+ * Repeated success performs no writes.
+ * A programming failure is terminal: partial register writes can have exposed
+ * the address, so the lease and its references remain retained. Does not
+ * enable the memif or its IRQ. This call sleeps.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_prepare(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer);
+
+/* After firmware PREPARE, program the disabled IRQ's counter, rate and active
+ * AFE clock domain. Requires successful address preparation and unchanged,
+ * non-running ALSA setup. Repeated success writes nothing. A write failure
+ * is terminal and retains the lease. Sets endpoint ABI 2's irq_prepared flag
+ * only after complete success. Does not enable or route the IRQ; sleeps.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_prepare_irq(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer);
+
+/* After acknowledged task STOPs, disable the owned memif, disable/clear
+ * its IRQ and remove its MCU and DSP target bits. The route argument is
+ * endpoint enum 2 for HiFi1 or 3 for primary HiFi5, not a task-core enum.
+ * Allows the still-running ALSA STOP callback, but requires
+ * unchanged ownership and
+ * format. Repeated success writes nothing; failed I/O is terminal. Does not
+ * prove whole-core quiescence; no published memory may be released. The caller
+ * serializes handle lifetime. This call sleeps.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_stop_irq(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer, unsigned int core);
+
+/* Forget a published lease's ALSA substream before that substream is freed.
+ * Caller first stops or abandons its task and synchronizes its callbacks.
+ * Retains the allocation, memif reservation and power/module references.
+ * Future endpoint/prepare operations fail. No MMIO or DMA release; sleeps.
+ */
+void mt8901_afe_sram_retire(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer);
+
+/* Call after binding and before publishing a buffer address to firmware or
+ * hardware. A published lease cannot be released by the current API and blocks
+ * AFE runtime suspend. System sleep requires every owner
+ * to participate in the retained-SRAM protocol.
+ * Service acknowledgements do not establish whole-core DMA quiescence.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_publish(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer);
+
+/* Release an unpublished lease. EBUSY leaves a published handle and all its
+ * resources intact. Otherwise consumes the handle; a negative runtime-PM
+ * result reports a suspend failure after the lease itself has been released.
+ * The caller serializes operations on each handle. This call sleeps.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_release(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer);
+
+/* Retained system-sleep protocol for published DSP-owned SRAM. The owner must
+ * have a DSP -> AFE PM link and participate in the sound card's ASoC ordering.
+ * allow_retention() is a capability declaration during successful setup.
+ * suspend() follows acknowledged DSP D3 and a stopped ALSA stream; resume()
+ * follows restored AFE SRAM and acknowledged DSP D0. Neither releases memory.
+ */
+int mt8901_afe_sram_allow_retention(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer);
+int mt8901_afe_sram_suspend(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer);
+int mt8901_afe_sram_resume(struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer *buffer);
+
+#endif
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/sound/n1x_adsp_client.h
@@ -0,0 +1,218 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
+#ifndef N1X_ADSP_CLIENT_H
+#define N1X_ADSP_CLIENT_H
+
+#include "n1x_adsp_ipc.h"
+#include "n1x_adsp_pcm.h"
+
+struct device;
+struct n1x_adsp_primary;
+struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer;
+struct snd_pcm_substream;
+
+#ifdef __KERNEL__
+#include <linux/acpi.h>
+#include <linux/platform_device.h>
+
+/* Referenced unique sibling in the consumer's firmware scope. NULL consumer
+ * is reserved for standalone validation modules and requires global uniqueness.
+ * Never pick the first device when firmware associations are ambiguous.
+ */
+static inline struct device *n1x_adsp_find_device(struct device *consumer, const char *hid)
+{
+	struct acpi_device *adev = NULL, *found = NULL;
+	struct acpi_device *parent = NULL;
+	struct device *dev;
+
+	if (consumer) {
+		if (!ACPI_COMPANION(consumer))
+			return NULL;
+		parent = acpi_dev_parent(ACPI_COMPANION(consumer));
+		if (!parent)
+			return NULL;
+	}
+	while ((adev = acpi_dev_get_next_match_dev(adev, hid, NULL, -1))) {
+		if (consumer && acpi_dev_parent(adev) != parent)
+			continue;
+		if (found) {
+			acpi_dev_put(found);
+			acpi_dev_put(adev);
+			return NULL;
+		}
+		found = acpi_dev_get(adev);
+	}
+	if (!found)
+		return NULL;
+	dev = bus_find_device_by_acpi_dev(&platform_bus_type, found);
+	acpi_dev_put(found);
+	return dev;
+}
+#endif
+
+#define N1X_ADSP_PRIMARY_ABI 3U
+
+/* Query the typed PCM client contract before opening a task. No firmware
+ * access. ABI 3 adds route-3 HiFi5 capture, DL1 playback and independent duplex
+ * owners to ABI 2's retained-ring and STOP/PREPARE/START contract.
+ */
+__u32 n1x_adsp_primary_abi(void);
+
+struct n1x_adsp_primary_pcm_params {
+	__u32 rate, channels, sample_bits, period_frames, periods;
+};
+
+struct n1x_adsp_primary_pcm_view {
+	void *area;
+	size_t bytes;
+};
+
+struct n1x_adsp_ipc_reply {
+	__u8 packet[N1X_ADSP_IPC_BYTES];
+};
+
+/* Kernel service clients supply token=0 and ack_mode=1. The transport assigns
+ * the token and serializes each request through its matching acknowledgment.
+ * A successful exchange does not establish service success or DMA quiescence.
+ * The client validates the service reply and retains any published buffers
+ * until that service's release contract is satisfied. Errors are not retryable.
+ * The reply is unchanged on error. This call sleeps and requires process context.
+ * Tasks 7/16 and 23/21 must use the dedicated PCM lifecycle API below.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_transfer(struct device *dev,
+		      const struct n1x_adsp_ipc_request *request,
+		      struct n1x_adsp_ipc_reply *reply);
+
+/* Register the primary task's four message buffers: task 7 on route 2
+ * (HiFi1 playback), or task 23 on route 3 (primary HiFi5 capture). The core
+ * and firmware endpoint properties must agree. Registered buffers
+ * remain owned by the DSP boot allocation; this call does not open a stream.
+ * Repeated calls after success reuse the registration. A failed sequence
+ * cannot be replayed or release its buffers. This call sleeps.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_prepare_primary(struct device *dev);
+
+/* Open the primary task exclusively after registering its message buffers.
+ * Returns an owned handle or ERR_PTR(). No PCM configuration or START is sent.
+ * A failed firmware request prevents reopening until device reinitialization.
+ * Successful HWFREE/CLOSE permits reopening with the same retained buffers.
+ * This call sleeps and requires process context.
+ */
+struct n1x_adsp_primary *n1x_adsp_primary_open(struct device *dev);
+
+/* ALSA frontend variant. Validates an AFE-owned DL0/DL1 playback or UL1
+ * capture substream and retains a card-to-DSP system-PM link until close. Even an unconfigured open
+ * stream is ordered before DSP D3. Legacy open() clients have no such grant.
+ * Does not bypass the exclusive OPEN, firmware or lifetime checks; sleeps.
+ */
+struct n1x_adsp_primary *n1x_adsp_primary_open_pcm(struct device *dev,
+						   struct snd_pcm_substream *substream);
+
+/* Reattach the persistent AFE ring after successful HWFREE/CLOSE and a fresh
+ * OPEN. ENOENT means no ring exists yet; reserve/bind an initial lease instead.
+ * No firmware request, allocation or release. Requires serialized ALSA setup.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_rebind(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary,
+			    struct snd_pcm_substream *substream);
+
+/* Register and open processing task 16 (playback, SRAM messages) or task 21
+ * (capture, boot-owned DRAM messages), then configure the primary host ring,
+ * processing AFE ring and bridge with
+ * commands 4, 0x201 and 4. Sends no PREPARE or START. The AFE must remain in
+ * non-running stream setup, serialized by the caller. Host and AFE formats
+ * must match; period sizes/counts may differ. Missing AFE support is rejected
+ * before any firmware request. A firmware-stage failure is terminal.
+ *
+ * After successful rebind, pass *sram=NULL to reuse the retained ring.
+ * Otherwise, on publication, ownership of *sram transfers to the DSP boot state and
+ * *sram becomes NULL, including if the following request fails. Otherwise
+ * the caller still owns its lease. Published memory remains retained until
+ * verified whole-core shutdown, which is not implemented yet. A failure before
+ * PCM publication can still retain published IPC SRAM. This call sleeps.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_configure(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary,
+			       const struct n1x_adsp_primary_pcm_params *params,
+			       struct mt8901_afe_sram_buffer **sram);
+
+/* Prepare the processing task with commands 0x203 (hardware) and 3 (bridge),
+ * then the primary task with commands 0x203 and 3 (both host). Revalidates the
+ * published AFE endpoint during non-running ALSA setup;
+ * the caller serializes setup/teardown. Repeated success sends no further IPC.
+ * A firmware-stage failure is terminal and retains both rings. This does not
+ * enable the AFE memif, start a stream or release DMA. Before DSP PREPARE,
+ * the AFE owner programs its memif address with checked writes.
+ * After all four acknowledgements, the owner prepares the disabled IRQ's
+ * period counter, rate and active clock domain. Requires AFE endpoint ABI 2.
+ * A programming failure is terminal. This call sleeps.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_prepare_pcm(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary);
+
+/* Return the configured coherent host-ring view to its owning kernel client.
+ * Valid only for this handle's lifetime. No userspace mapping is provided.
+ * The output is unchanged on error. This call sleeps.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_pcm_view(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary,
+			      struct n1x_adsp_primary_pcm_view *view);
+
+/* Publish a prepared playback host ring's write cursor after filling samples
+ * through pcm_view. The caller owns availability and serializes sample writes/handle
+ * lifetime. byte_offset is frame-aligned and may equal the ring size.
+ * Orders completed sample writes before the registered descriptor, preserving
+ * the last validated read address and advancing the write-generation counter.
+ * Sends no mailbox command. A late power error can follow publication; that
+ * error is terminal and the client must not retry or release published memory.
+ * Capture rejects this call with EOPNOTSUPP. Requires process context; sleeps.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_commit(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary, __u32 byte_offset);
+
+/* Start the prepared route-2 task-16/task-7 playback or route-3 task-21/23
+ * capture chain. Playback requires published samples; both require AFE
+ * endpoint ABI 2 IRQ readiness. The Linux
+ * audio client owns its DAPM/codec routing; this call does not program a gain
+ * or channel merge or enable a CPU memif. Repeated success sends no IPC.
+ * Firmware-stage failures are terminal and may leave hardware active.
+ * Sleeps; the caller serializes sample, stream and handle lifetime.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_start(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary);
+
+/* STOP the primary then processing task, then disable/clear the owned IRQ. Successful
+ * repetition sends no IPC or register writes. Synchronizes and detaches the
+ * period listener; the client must drain its own queued work before freeing
+ * listener data. Does not release memory or prove core quiescence. Restart
+ * requires a fresh PREPARE, listener and, for playback, sample publication; no buffers are freed.
+ * A failed request is terminal. Requires process context; sleeps.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_stop(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary);
+
+/* Register one playback-consumed or capture-produced data listener, or pass NULL to detach it. The listener runs
+ * in IRQ context and must not sleep or call sleeping DSP APIs. Its position
+ * snapshot is valid only during the call. A negative error reports a rejected
+ * notification; no buffer address from that packet is used.
+ * One message does not necessarily correspond to one ALSA period.
+ * Detach and close wait for in-flight IRQ callbacks before returning, so the
+ * caller may then free listener data. Do not hold a lock needed by the listener.
+ * Drain work queued by the listener separately before freeing its data.
+ * Requires process context and serialized handle lifetime. This call sleeps.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_set_period(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary,
+			       void (*period)(void *data,
+					      const struct n1x_adsp_pcm_position *position,
+					      int error), void *data);
+
+/* Copy the latest consumed position after prepare. Before the first notification,
+ * valid is false and the offset is zero. Returns a cached notification/transport error
+ * without changing the output. May be called from IRQ context while the caller
+ * retains the handle; this does not acknowledge or publish any firmware data.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_position(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary,
+			     struct n1x_adsp_pcm_position *position);
+
+/* Stop a started stream, then send primary HWFREE/CLOSE and, if opened,
+ * processing HWFREE/AFE-HWFREE/CLOSE, stopping at the first error.
+ * Consumes the handle on
+ * every result; the caller must not use it again. Published DMA remains owned
+ * by the DSP driver. Failure leaves the task unavailable for another open.
+ * This call sleeps and requires process context.
+ */
+int n1x_adsp_primary_close(struct n1x_adsp_primary *primary);
+
+#endif
